### Run your first automated video creation

Now that all credentials are configured, you're ready to create your first video:
1. Go to your Airtable base.
2. In the "Inspirational videos" table, create a new record.
3. For the "Topic" field, enter a motivational topic, for example: "The importance of believing in yourself".
4. For the "Language" field, enter "English".
5. For the "Voice Name" field, enter "en-US-JennyMultilingualNeural".
6. For the "Voice Model" field, enter "azure".
7. For the "Title Font" field, enter "Oswald Bold".
8. For the "Image Model" field, enter "flux-schnell".
9. For the "Subtitles Model" field, enter "default".
10. For the "Subtitles Font" field, enter "Oswald Bold".
11. For the "Music URL" field, enter "https://cdn.json2video.com/assets/audios/inspirational-03.mp3".
12. Ensure the "Status" field is set to "Todo".
13. Save the record.
14. Go back to your Make.com scenario.
15. Click on the "Run once" button (usually at the bottom-center or top-right of the scenario builder).
16. The workflow will start processing. First, it will fetch the "Todo" record from Airtable. Then, OpenAI will generate the content. Next, JSON2Video will create the video. Finally, the "Wait for a Movie to Render" module will wait for the video to be ready.
17. Once the scenario finishes running, go back to your Airtable base.
18. The "Status" field for your record should now be "Done", and the "Result" field will be populated with the URL to your newly generated video. Click on the URL to watch your inspirational video!

## Localizing your videos into other languages

One of the powerful aspects of this automation is its ability to localize your inspirational videos into various languages. This means you can reach a global audience with content tailored to their native tongue, enhancing relatability and impact. The process involves adjusting a few key fields in your Airtable record.

### Example: creating a video in Arabic

Let's create an inspirational video with a Korean voiceover and subtitles, demonstrating how to handle non-western charsets:
1. In your Airtable "Inspirational videos" table, create a new record.
2. For the "Topic" field, enter something inspiring, like: "Mental Toughness - Training your mind for adversity.".
3. For the "Language" field, enter "Arabic".
4. For the "Voice Name" field, enter "en-US-OnyxTurboMultilingualNeural". This voice is multilingual, so it can speak in Arabic as well. You can find a [full list of supported Azure voices by language here](https://json2video.com/ai-voices/azure/languages/).
5. For the "Voice Model" field, ensure it is set to "azure".
6. For the "Title Font" field, enter "Noto Sans Arabic". This font supports the Arabic character set. Remember that the font you choose must support the target language's characters. You can explore [Google Fonts](https://fonts.google.com/) for suitable options.
7. For the "Image Model" field, enter "flux-schnell".
8. For the "Subtitles Model" field, enter "whisper". Arabic is not supported by the default transcription model, so we use Whisper instead.
9. For the "Subtitles Font" field, enter "Arial". This is a simple font that supports the Arabic character set.
10. For the "Music URL" field, you can use the same URL as before: "[https://cdn.json2video.com/assets/audios/inspirational-05.mp3](https://cdn.json2video.com/assets/audios/inspirational-05.mp3)".
11. Set the "Status" field to "Todo".
12. Run the Make.com scenario as described in the previous section.
13. Once complete, check the "Result" URL in Airtable. Your video will now feature an Arabic voiceover and Arabic subtitles, demonstrating effective localization!
[full list of supported Azure voices by language here](https://json2video.com/ai-voices/azure/languages/)
[Google Fonts](https://fonts.google.com/)
[https://cdn.json2video.com/assets/audios/inspirational-05.mp3](https://cdn.json2video.com/assets/audios/inspirational-05.mp3)
